{
  "schema": "SCH-QUA-001",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "workPackage": "DAT-001",
  "workPackageTitle": "Common definition envelope, stable-ID rules, schema infrastructure, diagnostic format",
  "notes": [
    "Entries are added before implementation and are never renumbered (docs/technical/91 § Verification registry).",
    "Fixture IDs are file names beneath tests/MechaMiner.Content.Tests/Fixtures/. Every invalid fixture asserts the one diagnostic code it is named for; a fixture that fails with a different code fails the suite, because a gate that passes on the wrong error is not a gate.",
    "VER-DAT-001-022 is the over-strict control: the valid fixtures must produce zero diagnostics. Without it the invalid corpus could be satisfied by a validator that rejects everything.",
    "VER-DAT-001-021 is the mechanism doc 40 § JSON codec and schema baseline asks for by name: 'a fixture corpus proves the schema and typed validator accept/reject the same structural cases'. The typed validator stays authoritative; the draft 2020-12 schema is the interoperability mirror.",
    "VER-DAT-001-023 exists because a string field carrying a mini-language drifts unless its shape is pinned structurally. The envelope schema's source_refs pattern must reject a malformed element on its own, with the typed parser removed from the path.",
    "The size, depth, and count limits verified by VER-DAT-001-007 are injected rather than global, so a boundary fixture stays a small reviewable file instead of a megabyte of generated JSON. VER-DAT-001-007 also asserts the shipped default limit values.",
    "VER-DAT-001-026 and VER-DAT-001-027 exist because the failure this project keeps repeating is a control that covers only the routes its author enumerated by hand. 026 attacks the walk's reach position by position; 027 attacks the two ways a list-driven control fails silently - a keyword deleted from the list, and an empty set that satisfies every emptiness assertion.",
    "VER-DAT-001-028 and VER-DAT-001-029 continue that pass. 028 attacks the input set itself: a fixture no table row claims is tested by nothing, and a code proved by two fixtures can lose one while every set-equality assertion stays true. 029 attacks the walk's model of what a schema object is - every keyword is a legal property name, so a map keyed by author-chosen names cannot be read as a subschema.",
    "TR-DAT-003's full gate is DAT-006's ('source-order permutation yields identical hash' over a compiled bundle). VER-DAT-001-010 proves the same property at the single-payload level that DAT-006 builds on."
  ],
