      "summary": "The x-authority gate cannot be narrowed by deletion and cannot pass vacuously. The nine bound keywords are stated in the test independently of SchemaAuthority.BoundKeywords(), so removing one - which would delete the rule and every parameterised control for it in a single edit, leaving no exemption list behind - fails a test that names the keyword removed. Every bound keyword is asserted to be one the evaluator implements, so no control can pass on the wrong diagnostic. The walk over content/schemas is asserted to have visited a nonzero number of documents, objects, and bounds; the *.schema.json glob is asserted to match every JSON file in that directory; and both counts are proved to be real counts by a bound-free schema that reports zero bounds and an empty corpus that reports zero documents, each producing the same empty violation list a clean corpus does.",
