      "summary": "The structure-blind corpus walk reads a name-to-subschema map as a map and never as a subschema. Every schema keyword is a legal property name, so a properties, $defs, patternProperties or dependentSchemas map declaring a member called maximum beside one called x-authority presented the walk with a bound keyword and an authority keyword side by side: it counted a bound that does not exist and suppressed its own finding on it, and without the authority-named sibling it reported an unattributed bound at a pointer addressing no bound. The counted phantom is the fail-open, because BoundsSeen is what VER-DAT-001-027 relies on to prove the gate looked at anything. Asserted over every recognised keyword in each of the four map positions, so a keyword implemented later inherits the control, plus a committed fixture whose declared properties are named maximum, $defs, $ref, type and x-authority and whose one real unattributed bound must still be reported. The loader's structure-aware walk reads properties through ReadSubschemaMap and never had the confusion; it is asserted on the same fixture.",
